Note on H-third (equivalent; not a gap of the tests). The pending pair ((N/g) w', j + 1) of the third case of
Algorithm H (docs/proofs/solvers.md:635 to 637) is implied by what is already there. Proof: in the third case
g = gcd(a, h) = s a + t h, w' = s v + t w, v' = (h/g) v - (a/g) w, and v' stays pending at j + 1. By (I3) for
the old row w (solvers.md:665), (N/h) w is in the span U of the rows T[j'] with j' > j and of the pending vectors
at positions > j; U contains v' after the step, and later steps keep or enlarge the spans (proof of 2.5(2)).
Now (h/g) v = v' + (a/g) w, so (N/g) v = (N/h)(h/g) v = (N/h) v' + (a/g) (N/h) w is in U, and
(N/g) w = (h/g) (N/h) w is in U. Hence (N/g) w' = s (N/g) v + t (N/g) w is in U: (I3) for the new row w' holds
without the added pair. Probe: lanes/s1-slice1/probe_third_case.py, 34000 random row sets (N up to 3^9 2^5, up
to 5 columns, 7 rows), the third case taken 60577 times: 0 outputs differ from Algorithm H as written.
